# tests/ is excluded wholesale because the build context must not carry the test
# suite into the image. welcome-close-gate.sh is the one exception: it is a gate
# that runs against the INSTALLED system, so it has to ship, and it stays under
# tests/ because it is a test and must keep reading like one. Verified with a
# scratch build that this negation re-includes exactly this file and nothing
# else from tests/.
!tests/welcome-close-gate.sh

# The DN-48 LibreOffice parity gates, same reasoning. The .xcd checker runs at
# build time, and the UNO gate and its probe cannot: there is no LibreOffice to
# start inside a build layer, so they ship to be run against the installed
# system on the Dell or a VM, which is the only place the parity is real.
!tests/libreoffice-xcd-check.py
!tests/libreoffice-parity-gate.sh
!tests/libreoffice-parity-probe.py

# The Help application's gate, same reasoning again: it needs the help server
# running and a browser engine to drive, neither of which exists inside a build
# layer, so it ships to be run against the installed system.
!tests/help-app-gate.sh
!tests/help-app-probe.py
